{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790284128,"nonce":"W3tnwfnt7sRSs2C5t16Wq0uxxoE=","title":"wasm tier: a compiled body returns a string literal as its symbol index","message":"Reproducer, under wasm/web/node-run.mjs with the browser bundle:\n\n    var f = Fn.new {|i| \"lit\" }\n    var s = null\n    var k = 0\n    while (k \u003c 300) {\n      s = f.call(k)\n      k = k + 1\n    }\n    System.print(s)\n\nprints 2.0355504608659e-321 instead of lit: once f tiers up to wasm,\nthe literal is the Num whose bits are the literal's symbol index.\n\"a%(i)b\" renders the same way around the interpolated value, so\nMeta.eval of an interpolated source string fails to parse. Present in\nthe Sep 18 bundle and at bb2542c.\n\ncodegen/wasm.rs lowers Instruction::ConstString(idx) to i64.const idx;\nthe native backends call wren_const_string(idx), which allocates the\nstring. The fix is the same call (it allocates, so it is a collection\npoint for scan_roots_across).","files":null}]}